    {
      "fileName": "inescapable-grasp.json",
      "id": "UxjAszOYAhUvCDt2",
      "name": "Inescapable Grasp",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "UxjAszOYAhUvCDt2",
        "folder": "bcoviuaJ3aOakfIO",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Inescapable Grasp",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>Your grasp has a supernatural quality to it, preventing your foes from easily escaping—with or without magical assistance. If a creature you have @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Grabbed] attempts to use a teleportation spell or effect, it must succeed at a @Check[flat|dc:15] or the spell fails. If a creature you have grabbed attempts to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Escape] while under the effect of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Unfettered Movement] or a similar effect, it must succeed at a @Check[flat|dc:15] or be forced to roll the Escape attempt normally, rather than automatically succeeding.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Inescapable Grasp]</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 12
          },
          "prerequisites": {
